# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics is **already fully configured and operational** in this project. After fetching the latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart and reviewing the codebase, I confirmed that the implementation follows the official Next.js App Router setup exactly.

## Current Implementation

### 1. Package Installation ✅
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1
- **Location**: Listed in `package.json` dependencies
- **Status**: Already installed

### 2. Analytics Component Configuration ✅
- **File**: `web/src/app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
- **Import**: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- **Implementation**: The `<Analytics />` component is correctly placed within the `<body>` element of the root layout

### 3. Environment-Aware Loading ✅
The implementation includes a production best practice:
```typescript
{process.env.VERCEL_ENV && <Analytics />}
```

This conditional loading ensures:
- Analytics only loads when deployed on Vercel (when `VERCEL_ENV` is set)
- Prevents 404 errors in local development where the `/_vercel/insights` endpoint doesn't exist
- Avoids CSP (Content Security Policy) violations during local development
- Improves developer experience

